      "v": 4,
      "zh": "弯曲的心思，我必远离；一切的恶人（或译：恶事），我不认识。",
      "en": "I will have nothing to do with a perverse person;[NOTE:1] I will not permit[NOTE:2] evil.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “it [i.e., the doing of evil deeds] does not cling to me.”",
        "Heb “a perverse heart will turn aside from me.” The adjective עִקֵּשׁ (ʿiqqesh) has the basic nuance “twisted; crooked” and by extension refers to someone or something that is morally perverse (see Ps 18:26). It appears frequently in the Book of Proverbs, where it is used of evil people (22:5), speech (8:8; 19:1), thoughts (11:20; 17:20), and life styles (2:15; 28:6)."
      ],
